    <!-- Detailed help text in create Safe Box flow explaining the Location field. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.location.info.text">Location refers to a folder within your Koofr where all of your Safe Box files and folders are securely stored.\n\nIf this is your first Safe Box, the default location will be "My safe box." You can change it if you prefer.\n\nIf you already have a Safe Box or wish to use an existing folder (e.g. one created with rclone), you can select that folder.\n\nPlease note that you can only select a folder located within your Koofr.</string>
    <!-- Title of the location help sheet in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.location.info.title">Location</string>
    <!-- Section header label for storage location in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.location.label">Location</string>
    <!-- Placeholder shown when no location is selected in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.location.placeholder">Location</string>
    <!-- Accessibility label for the safe key help button in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.password.info.button.a11y.label">Safe Key info</string>
    <!-- Detailed help text in create Safe Box flow explaining the Safe Key field and recovery limitations. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.password.info.text">Safe Key is a password used to encrypt your files. Each Safe Box can have its own unique Safe Key.\n\nPlease be aware that once you set your Safe Key, it cannot be changed later. All the files within the Safe Box will be encrypted using this key.\n\nIMPORTANT: Your Safe Key cannot be reset, and there is no way to recover your files if you forget it, as it is never sent to or stored on Koofr servers.</string>
    <!-- Title of the safe key help sheet in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.password.info.title">Safe Key</string>
    <!-- Section header label for safe key input in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.password.label">Safe Key</string>
    <!-- Placeholder for the Safe Key field describing minimum length requirement. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.password.placeholder">Must be at least 8 characters long</string>
    <!-- Accessibility label for the salt input field in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.salt.a11y.label">Salt</string>
    <!-- Accessibility label for the salt help button in create Safe Box form. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.salt.info.button.a11y.label">Salt info</string>
    <!-- Detailed help text in create Safe Box flow explaining the Salt field. -->
    <string name="ios.repo_create.form.salt.info.text">Salt is used in the key derivation process to create a unique encryption key and helps to protect against potential attacks. It will be stored on the Koofr servers in a secure manner.\n\nA random Salt has been generated for you. If you prefer, you can leave the Salt field empty, and the default salt will be used (same as in rclone). However, it is recommended to use a unique salt for enhanced security. Using a unique salt helps to increase the complexity of the encryption process, making it more difficult for potential attackers to access the encrypted data.\n\nIf you wish to transfer the encrypted files to another service, it is necessary to also export the salt, otherwise you won\'t be able to decrypt your files.</string>
